WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:03.200
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.129
A servant has a method to steal wine.

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:11.519
He removes three cups from a barrel of wine and replaces it with 3 cups of water.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.100
The next day he wants more wine. So he does the same thing.

00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:25.679
He removes three cups from the same barrel that now contains diluted wine and replaces it with 3 cups of water.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:30.059
The following day he repeats this one more time.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:36.719
So he has drawn a total of three times from the same barrel and has poured back a total of nine cups of water.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.849
At this point the barrel is 50% wine and fifty percent water.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.250
The question is how many cups of wine were originally in the barrel?

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.189
This problem is a classic mathematical puzzle from the 16th century.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.370
Can you figure it out?

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:01.170
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:09.179
We'll get started with the barrel of wine.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:17.099
We're going to keep track of the number of cups of wine in the barrel and the concentration of wine in the barrel.

00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:24.689
At the beginning we'll denote the unknown amount of wine by the variable x cups.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:33.150
The barrel at first contains only wine, so it's concentration will be one or it's a hundred percent wine.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:41.220
The servant then removes three cups from the barrel and replaces it with 3 cups of water.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.530
The barrel will have a diluted amount of wine.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:53.520
We know that three cups of wine are removed so the total amount of wine remaining will be x minus 3.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.259
Since the servant has placed back in three cups of water

00:01:58.719 --> 00:02:02.819
the total amount of liquid in the barrel remains the same at x.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:10.429
So the concentration of wine will be the amount of wine x minus 3 divided by the total volume of liquid x.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:20.500
If we divide this through by x we have 1 minus 3 over x. It will be convenient to write it in this form.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.060
The next day the servant does the same thing

00:02:26.299 --> 00:02:29.049
so the wine and the barrel gets diluted even more.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:32.140
How much wine will be in the barrel?

00:02:32.329 --> 00:02:39.009
When we already have x minus 3 cups that are in there and then he removes 3 cups of the diluted wine.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:44.679
So the amount of wine remaining will be x minus 3 minus 3

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:50.798
times the diluted wine that he is removing. The concentration of the diluted wine

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:56.560
allows us to figure out the exact amount of wine that he's removing as opposed to water.

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:04.599
So we can now simplify this fraction to figure out the amount of wine that's remaining in the barrel.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.789
This will be x minus 6 plus 9 over x.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:18.549
Once again the total volume of liquid remains at x because the servant is replacing the wine that he removes with water.

00:03:20.329 --> 00:03:24.579
So the concentration of wine will be this amount of wine

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.019
divided by x.

00:03:27.019 --> 00:03:29.019
We can then divide through

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.639
and then we can actually see that we can factor this term.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:40.029
We end up with the concentration of 1 minus 3 over x, the quantity squared.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:47.079
So the following day the servant does this one more time, so the wine gets even more diluted?

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.560
So from the amount of wine in the previous day,

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:55.989
we subtract out three times the concentration of wine from the previous day.

00:03:58.579 --> 00:04:03.339
So we can simplify this fraction to figure out the amount of wine that's remaining in the barrel.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:09.190
This will be 9 minus x  plus 27 over x minus 27 over x squared.

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:17.649
This amount divided by the total volume x is how much of the wine concentration is remaining in the barrel.

00:04:18.289 --> 00:04:23.279
I'll go ahead and simplify this and it actually ends up being one minus 3 over x cubed.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.379
So that's the final concentration of wine now.

00:04:28.379 --> 00:04:32.039
We've gone through all this algebra, and I just want to point out there was a shortcut

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:34.469
we could have used if we had realized earlier.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:39.539
After we had gone through the first step of figuring out the concentration of wine,

00:04:39.819 --> 00:04:43.649
we could have noticed that the concentration going from one hundred percent

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:49.349
to the first step is found by multiplying by 1 minus 3 divided by x.

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:57.389
Now in order to get to the next concentration. We actually could have just multiplied by the same percentage

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.069
to get to the next concentration.

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:08.039
We could have done the same thing once more when we're looking at the concentration and we're iterating the same process the

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:10.408
concentrations get multiplied by each other.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:15.899
In any case we figured out the concentration of wine at the very end.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:20.009
And we are given this is equal to fifty percent.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.009
So we now have an algebra problem to solve.

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:30.119
We have the quantity 1 minus 3 over x cubed equal to one-half.

00:05:31.479 --> 00:05:37.139
We can take the cube root of each side, and then we can isolate and solve for the term x.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:45.810
We end up with x being equal to three times the cube root of 2 all divided by the cube root of 2 minus 1.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.039
And this gives us our answer that there were approximately

00:05:51.969 --> 00:05:56.519
14.54 cups of wine in the barrel to start with.

